# Web skeletons (`civil-web`)

Use the shadcn `Skeleton` primitive and shared presets — do not add packages like `react-loading-skeleton`.

## Source of truth

- Primitive: `@/components/ui/skeleton` (shadcn)
- Presets: `@/components/feedback/skeletons`
- Wire via `AsyncState` `loadingFallback` (default is `ContentSkeleton`)
- Mock screens: `loadMock(data)` + `useRemoteData` so skeletons are visible

## Preset map

| Layout | Preset | Use when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Generic | `ContentSkeleton` | Unknown / simple blocks |
| Card grid | `CardGridSkeleton` | Project/provider/directory cards |
| Card image | `CardImageSkeleton` / `CivilCardMedia` | Card media (wireframe civil art) |
| Stats | `StatGridSkeleton` | Dashboard / stat strips |
| Table | `TableSkeleton` | Logs, admin tables |
| Detail form | `DetailSkeleton` | Multi-card detail pages |
| Detail card | `DetailCardSkeleton` | Single key/value detail |
| List | `ListSkeleton` | Notification inbox rows |
| Gallery | `GallerySkeleton` | Image grids |

## Rules

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — spinner or empty card as “skeleton”
if (isLoading) return <p>Loading…</p>

// ✅ GOOD — AsyncState + matching preset
<AsyncState
  isLoading={remote.isLoading}
  error={remote.isError ? remote.error : undefined}
  onRetry={() => void remote.refetch()}
  loadingFallback={<TableSkeleton columns={5} />}
>
  {children}
</AsyncState>
```

- Match skeleton shape to loaded UI.
- Every list/table/detail/analytics page that loads data must use `AsyncState` + a preset.
- `InlineSpinner` only for brief auth/session hydration.
- Keep `PageHeader` outside the loading fallback when possible.
